Subject: WebView: start the WebView zygote with the first renderer, not at boot

WebViewUpdateService started the WebView zygote on a background thread as soon as WebView's
RELRO files were made (SystemImpl.ensureZygoteStarted, which only calls
WebViewZygote.getProcess), so a boot with no app that shows web content still held the zygote,
5 to 7 MiB of PSS, for the whole session.

ensureZygoteStarted now does nothing. WebViewZygote.getProcess, which the activity manager calls
to start each renderer, starts the zygote when there is none and keeps it from then on, as
before. The first WebView of a boot waits a few hundred milliseconds once for the zygote's
start. make-image.py made this change as a dex edit of the published services.jar until the
image took the framework build's.

Applies to frameworks/base at 94b4c163b7dfe5ce3607f7bb8456f9573f7de57d (Android 17).
---
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/webkit/SystemImpl.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/webkit/SystemImpl.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/webkit/SystemImpl.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/webkit/SystemImpl.java
@@ -252,7 +252,10 @@ public class SystemImpl implements SystemInterface {

     @Override
     public void ensureZygoteStarted() {
-        WebViewZygote.getProcess();
+        // DSA: the WebView zygote starts the first time an app needs a WebView renderer, not
+        // as soon as WebView's RELRO files are made. Started here, it held 5 to 7 MiB for the
+        // whole session of a boot no app showed web content in. WebViewZygote.getProcess, which
+        // the activity manager calls to start each renderer, starts it when there is none.
     }

     @Override
